+# Outdoor population first cut
+
+Adds55noncombat residents using existing native sprites and ten reusable Story conversations. Total75outdoor people, one or more in all54sections. Every new resident has a bounded one-axis range1walk. The existing20entries/local IDs remain exact; existing8trainer identities/battle roles remain separate. This checkpoint precedes the separately qualified3generic trainer patrols and Gameplay’s old-object-cache compatibility slice.
+
+The retained compiler exports movement fields and checks same-map routes, broad walkable bypasses, clearance from every door/sign/capture/oldContinue target and bridge approaches. The city stays connected even with every patrol route blocked simultaneously.55exact map/local-ID/graphics/movement/alternate-route contracts are in actors.json.
+
+All graphics, collision, warp and sign files are byte-identical to12104dc2; only54native map object lists append. Native full build and actual English/Traditional Chinese talk→release→resumed walking→player escape pass. Runtime dialogue bytes match localized ELF data exactly. Evidence: /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/qa/2026-11-24-boulevard-npcs/{resident-en-runtime,resident-zh-runtime,source-proof,population-proof}.json. Chinese and English player-view screenshots alongside.
+
+Uniform15×10viewport coverage17.02% vs4.65%; maximum2spawn actors in thatviewport,3in17×17draw area,4in one native map (plus player remains below16object slots). This is map coverage, not a typical player-route encounter probability.
+
+Story dependencies:abfa9fd8/ac460097 and matching glyph-safe pool metadata. Mechanical native macro export fix:0feb7066. Main owns combined cartridge/cache compatibility and publication.
+
+The patrol follow-up changes only the three generic manual trainers: RunwayJogger V1, NorthStudent H1 and GreenwayWalker V1. Greenway moves one tile north to preserve a complete broad bypass. All local IDs, trainer identities, script bindings and settings stay unchanged. Exact new/old anchors and cache contracts are in trainer-patrols.json. Full route/border source checks and census pass:75total,58walking,17stationary. Gameplay owns actual battle/facing/return qualification and old-cache extension before combined preview acceptance.
