+# Character-first gym dialogue
+
+Authored against protected preview f7e7d04d03f22872dad17fbd6bff88d5e1dd4897. Ten active leaders, including Wenyi/Confucius at slot5 and Muqing/Wanhe at slot8 (legacy MapleGarden symbol retained). Each new intro is at most two short native pages and replaces the corresponding existing IntroEn/Zh literal. Native trainerbattle automatically reads both pages before battle; no ASM flow change is needed for this copy.
+
+New TaichungGym_Text_*LeaderWinEn/Zh constants mean the leader won and the player lost. TaichungGymGetLeaderWinText(gymId) is a pure language-aware selector, returning empty for invalidgymIDs. Gameplay owns the actual matching-leader/player-loss gate and blackout/timing integration. Do not use these as leader-defeat or badge-award lines.
+
+Existing Defeat, Complete, Already, Loss/retry and all other source bytes stay unchanged. No progression, battle logic, ASM, menu, party, map or art changes. Natural original fictional voices; no copied commercial dialogue or new historical claims. Exact bilingual text is in dialogue.json. Font extension is separate: append nineteen pinned bitmap glyphs without renumbering existing1053entries. Main owns final pairing/review.
+
+Arrival follow-up on b9a98911: all ten introductions now acknowledge arrival and name the current gym location within the same two compact pages. The exact JSON replaces the earlier proof. All leader-wins text and its pure selector are unchanged. One separate append-only glyph companion adds 訪 after the existing1072entries. No script, battle, award, revisit, map or capture changes.
