+The Main save entry points call Gameplay's real
+`TaichungEncounterInitSaveState()` only when all three named reserved fields
+are zero. Gameplay remains the single writer of the schema and initial masks;
+Main does not copy its magic value or current mask into the entry policy.
+
+New game authenticates its own cleared save. Continue authenticates a nonempty
+party plus an existing map-save version1..12, or the exact pre-existing
+unversioned prototype recognition (four known starters, or a zero starter
+marker plus the tea marker). Untouched/unrecognized FireRed, empty-party
+Continue, and future map versions cannot initialize. The current-v12 path
+initializes before its migration early return, so this feature needs no new
+map version. Known schema and masks—including high bits and inconsistent raw
+unlock bits—remain byte-exact. Any nonzero unknown/corrupt reserved state is
+preserved without calling the initializer.
+
+Both entry points reset the transient encounter session, including all early
+returns. Ordinary map returns do not gain new calls. The Gameplay initializer
+publishes its schema last; failed or ignored schema writes leave virgin state
+unready and a subsequent authenticated Continue can retry. New initialization
+does not persist an attempt, grant an unlock, save to disk, or acknowledge a
+browser durability request.
