+model intentionally does not claim native SRAM offsets. All256 variables,
+party/bag-sized protected data, objects, padding, current/return/checkpoint
+positions and native pending-warp behavior are compared. Cases include
+source versions0..12 and future values, authenticated/unrecognized prototypes,
+empty parties, repeated entry, all65536 raw16-bit attempt masks with varied
+unlock/high bits, each ordered write failing or being ignored, retry after
+current-version early return, and all transient phases. The engine's zeroed
+new-save precondition is exercised separately.
