+FinalXitun delegates back to the current streets checker. The legacy view therefore retains its original actual inputs in a dict projection. The current streets boundary re-proves those original inputs and verifies the projection is exactly the authorized five-map substitution before unwrapping it. It never treats an ordinary mutation dict as a historical view. Corrupted/stale projections, altered nonstaff values and mismatched source paths reject; current corruption cannot be hidden by feeding an unmarked baseline map override.
