+# Landmark encounters and capture unlocks
+
+Built from published native6ae533a. The existing ten gym leader teams, badges,
+curated moves and warning remain authoritative. This slice changes no map
+geometry, facade, door or collision. Its first binding follows the existing
+Wenchang Temple host's optional history interaction. Main owns save initialization,
+browser persistence, build pairing, portable patch, integration PR and publication.
+
+`TaichungEncounter_Interact` takes a stable site ID in VAR_0x8004. Named wrappers
+for all14sites are in `data/scripts/taichung_encounters.inc`; Maps can bind them to
+new positions. `data/taichung/encounters/sites.json` lists the fixed species/levels,
+entry labels and current binding without assigning coordinates to future sites.
+
+Prepare team opens the existing Team menu and returns to the offer; Later/B leaves.
+Neither consumes a try or saves. Begin requires a healthy partner, no replay/battle,
+an initialized dedicated schema and an unused site. It consumes the site's bit,
+performs a real native SAVE_NORMAL and waits for the exact browser durable ACK
+before creating the wild mon. This explicit path bypasses random-wild preferences.
+
+The14allocated target species need their own capture unlock for future Team
+choices. Other original001–150 species remain free; Mew/later species are excluded.
+Existing saved parties are retained and usable even when a member's species is now
+locked. A locked selection shows its encounter place; it cannot replace a slot.
+Scyther remains available and has native GenIII False Swipe in its curated set.
+
+In these battles the BAG action becomes BALL with the number remaining. It emits
+GREAT BALL directly and spends one of3transient supplies when the action executes.
+No normal ball/item inventory is added or removed. Native Great Ball capture odds,
+status/HP modifiers, RNG and animation are retained. A successful native throw
+records capture provenance and unlocks only the matching species at battle end;
+there is no party append, replacement, nickname or PC deposit. Seen/caught flags
+may be updated by that genuine catch, but are never used to infer unlocks.
+
+The third failed throw ends the attempt. KO, run, loss, exhaustion and interruption
+have separate messages and no unlock. Run leaves immediately. Loss recovers the
+existing team and returns to the encounter script without a stock whiteout/prize
+loss. Normal battle HP/PP changes otherwise remain normal. Targets have authored
+non-recoil/non-escape moves, with a harmless recoil-free fallback instead of enemy
+Struggle after an unusually long restricted-move stall. Leaders remain three mons.
+
+Results perform another native save and wait for a separate durable ACK before
+releasing the field script. Without a consumer or durable storage there is no
+unsaved fallback battle. `include/taichung_encounter_bridge.h` documents the exact
+64-byte packet. ACK must match request sequence, attempted/unlocked masks and the
+just-written native flash generation; browser writes ACK sequence last. Main's
+client must exclude earlier whole-CPU snapshots and enforce native-SRAM Continue
+on refresh throughout the critical encounter. Host ACK models do not prove browser
+durability; Main's actual IndexedDB/reload/native Continue checks remain required.
+
+Dedicated vars: schema0x40F3 (marker0xEC01), attempted0x40F4, unlocked0x40F5,
+stable bits0–13. Main calls `TaichungEncounterInitSaveState` only for authenticated
+empty new/legacy state, preserves current masks and unknown/nonzero state, and
+calls `TaichungEncounterResetSession` at native new-game/Continue boundaries. No
+map save-version change belongs to this feature. Before initialized state, the
+offer declines safely. The normal Pokédex caught flags from the old free picker
+grant no new unlocks. Discarding/importing a save is an explicit save change, not
+an automatic retry; Main owns the associated browser boot-intent policy.
+
+Focused checks: `test-encounter.sh`, `test-encounter-bridge.sh`,
+`test-encounter-field.sh`, `test-team.sh`, `validate-team-presets.py` and
+`audit-encounter-slice.py`. Field tests use the actual adapter and real native
+headers with modeled engine/storage calls. They do not claim a GBA build, actual
+capture outcome or browser persistence acceptance. Main builds one exact matched
+ROM/ELF/bridge pair, then coordinates the browser lease and genuine-input QA.
