+# Named Xitun landmarks: placement and map bindings
+
+Source baseline: released native `a701ed5109ffd5eddd6b0581ade46591146e9656`. This component implements only National Trade Center/Magneton21, Ding Sheng BHW/Kabutops22 and The Lin/Persian23. The existing market, Huimin Park and civic-housing infill remain ordinary scenery with no new encounter IDs or landmark pins.
+
+The user authorized moving the two approved 8×13-metatile towers one tile outward within the same lot. Ding Sheng is now `[75,113,83,126]`; National Trade Center is `[87,113,95,126]`. Their PNGs, 13-tile height, frontage row and native collision derived from the original alpha are retained. Lamps move into the outer columns of the gap at `[83,119]` and `[86,119]`. Two independent signposts occupy `[83,124]` and `[86,124]`; centre columns84–85 stay clear from the north sidewalk through the south sidewalk.
+
+![Compiled tower spacing](tower-spacing-review.png)
+
+![Native player view](walk-tower-gap-player.png)
+
+## Stable interactions
+
+| Place | Native key | Local interaction | Local approach | Authored world interaction / approach | Map-owned script |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| National Trade Center, ID21 | 43:36 | `[14,16]` | `[14,17]` | `[86,124]` / `[86,125]` | `TaichungLandmark_NationalTradeCenter` |
+| Ding Sheng BHW, ID22 | 43:36 | `[11,16]` | `[11,17]` | `[83,124]` / `[83,125]` | `TaichungLandmark_DingShengBHW` |
+| The Lin, ID23 | 43:29 | `[18,13]` | `[18,14]` | `[57,140]` / `[57,141]` | `TaichungLandmark_TheLin` |
+
+The Lin reuses the existing citizen beside its entrance; its facade, lot, NPC graphics, standing position and collision do not change. Both sign wrappers and the guide invoke the existing common capture interaction with the stable ID. Gameplay owns registry availability/species and Story owns prose; this component does not implement those registries or claim completed capture battles before their integration.
+
+`data/taichung/named-xitun-bindings/anchors.json` gives native/local envelopes, exact source-art hashes and separate real visitor addresses and browsable sources. The address for NTC is **市政北二路282號**, as recorded by the [Taichung environmental bureau](https://green.epb.taichung.gov.tw/page/stronghold/p03.aspx?city=160&num=5952&pro_kind=2). Authored world x minus31 is the existing website/radar x; y is unchanged. Game coordinates are not GPS.
+
+## Compiled and native checks
+
+- All340 baseline generated native files reproduce the release reference byte for byte.
+- **227,652 resolved map/border cells** compared. All **211 changed world cells** lie inside `[75,113,95,126]`; other map pixels/collision remain identical. The Lin changes only its interaction-script binding.
+- All54 maps,40,039 walkable cells and186 directed connections remain reachable. Palette/graphics limits remain13/13 and778/1,011 in the worst 17×17 camera window;1,552/2,048 metatiles.
+- Actual mGBA controller sweeps pass on foot and bike: tower area441 tiles,1,518 directed steps and88 wall probes per mode across six native maps; The Lin56 tiles,164 steps and17 probes per mode. Zero failures.
+- Both physical sign interactions and the hotel guide reach their exact IDs on foot and bike. Native UI opens through the common interaction. New capture availability remains Gameplay's integration responsibility.
+
+## Continue dependency
+
+The tower move newly blocks **25 exact previously walkable cells**, all on43:36. `tower-source-proof.json` enumerates them and same-map stable target suggestions. Every earlier North infill repair destination remains walkable. The separate following Continue component extends the single existing generator/table to95 entries while preserving all prior70 rows. **Integrate that repair before publishing this geometry.** No bounding-box relocation or save-schema bump is required.
+
+## HD handoff
+
+The read-only `export_named_xitun_hd_anchors.py` rerenders the current compiled references using the verified web reader. `tower-hd-handoff.json` records exact changed pixels and full/partial tower coverage. Regenerate references **43.27,43.28,43.29,43.35,43.36,43.37**. All changed reference pixels map to this same tower lot.
+
+On43.36 (margin8), fresh full reference envelopes are Ding Sheng `[176,208,128,208]` and NTC `[368,208,128,208]`; core-local envelopes are `[48,80,128,208]` and `[240,80,128,208]`. Approved HD picture bytes and native art hashes are unchanged. Recompute coverage masks against the new references. Do not reuse the old manual positions/masks. Nine full/partial per-reference overlap records are supplied; the prior pack contains complete manual tower entries on43.36, while partial seam views are explicitly inventoried for Main's coverage policy.
+
+Main owns HD-pack, overview/radar/marker regeneration, combined Continue acceptance and publication. The Confucius gym / legacy Shen Ji room and moved Alakazam binding are separate follow-up work.
