+# Exact v12 Continue repair for North Xitun
+
+## Current integrated table — November 24
+
+The active table now contains **95 exact repairs**: the original 70 remain unchanged, and 25 newly blocked cells on `43:36` cover the approved tower spacing change. The additional baseline blob is from the live `a701ed51` cartridge. The generator verifies each open-to-solid change and same-map stable target against native collision words; `preserved-70-repairs.json` freezes all earlier source/target pairs.
+
+The existing helper, save version 12, and both Continue hooks are unchanged. The expanded compiled-helper suite passes **27,884 cases**, including ordinary and pending destinations, door/return priority, idempotence and protected save bytes. Maps' actual ordinary-save and pending/control emulator results are recorded separately under `artifacts/qa/2026-11-24-confucius-xitun/continue95/`; Main's final paired browser acceptance is a separate release check.
+
+## Original November 23 repair and acceptance
+
+The approved infill makes 70 formerly walkable cells solid: 37 on `TaichungBlvdXitunC1` (`43:27`) and 33 on `TaichungBlvdXitunC2` (`43:35`). Ordinary production v12 saves can resume inside those objects; 27 of these cells have no adjacent current walkable cell. Clearing the Boulevard map cache alone does not repair a saved position.
+
+This slice is based on Main's `6a108f44638b8b1d69cba271474e6713cc05b37c`. It adds a separate `TaichungNorthXitunRepairOnContinue` helper immediately after the existing upgrade in both native Continue callbacks. It keeps `src/taichung_save.c`, `include/taichung_save.h`, save version12 and all map/visual data unchanged. Removing the one new include and two callback calls restores Main's exact `overworld.c` bytes.
+
+For an authenticated version12 save with a partner, the helper matches only the exact 70 map/local coordinates. An ordinary Continue uses the actual saved `pos`, rather than the last arrival's `location.x/y`, and requests the existing complete Continue warp reload. A pending explicit Continue target is repaired only if it matches that same table. Native door/return warp IDs, safe pending destinations and all other positions retain priority. Future/unknown versions and no-party saves are untouched. The helper has no mutable globals and writes only the selected Continue target and its existing pending bit; it does not edit party, HP/PP, inventory, encounters, badges, preferences, checkpoint, other warp records or map data.
+
+## Source truth
+
+`data/taichung/north-xitun-continue/baseline/` retains the exact two pre-infill production map blobs from `0e9363298301c83f0db7e7b1bf3d44d918be5b20`. Their identity was checked against Git, and their hashes/geometry are recorded in `baseline.json`. The generator compares their native collision words with the current compiled maps and derives only open→solid cells.
+
+For each source, BFS follows old walkable ground to the nearest stable open cell in the same map, excluding NPCs, signs and warps and requiring an available next step. Ties use south/west/east/north order. Repairs move1–4 tiles: 39 move1, 16 move2, 13 move3 and2 move4. `repairs.json` is the readable source record; `src/data/taichung/north_xitun_continue.h` is generated const ROM data. No map-wide shift or v13 migration is introduced.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/boulevard_city/north_xitun_continue.py
+python3 -B tools/taichung/boulevard_city/test_north_xitun_continue.py
+```
+
+The first command verifies the complete table against old/current native cells. The second compiles the actual native helper against the existing host model: **21,536 cases** cover every cell in both maps, ordinary and pending targets, idempotence, native return priority, other maps/groups/versions, no-party saves and byte-for-byte protected SaveBlock1 state. It also verifies hook order in both ordinary and quest-log Continue callbacks.
+
+The full native ROM build passes. No additional EWRAM state is allocated. The old exact-source SaveC/header remain unchanged, so Main can preserve its existing qualification chain; the standalone historical encounter-init guard already reports the same newer-Gameplay-layer mismatch on unmodified Main6a108 and is not changed by this slice.
+
+## Native regression and genuine production saves
+
+QA lives under `/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/qa/2026-11-23-north-xitun-continue/`. **16 actual mGBA Continue cases passed** against the unpatched Main6a108 and repaired cartridges: genuine ordinary old saves, six pending explicit-target fixtures, and three safe/other-map controls. Repaired arrivals reach their exact expected cells and can walk away; safe positions remain unchanged. Saved/live party bytes, flags/vars, encounter state, badges, language, identity/options and other warp records match between the two cartridges. Currency and bag quantities match after native XOR decoding because a full reload legitimately re-randomizes their encryption key. A separate native read verifies deliberately depleted **HP7 and move1 PP1** survive.
+
+The ordinary old saves were generated by loading isolated bootstraps in the real production0e cartridge and using its native Save menu. That advanced the save counter2→3, cleared the pending-Continue flag and wrote consistent native object caches. They were not coordinate-patched after native Save. All relevant sector checksums and the partner checksum were independently verified. Read-only immutable copies and hashes are inventoried in `ordinary-production-saves.json`; these are distinct from the pending-coordinate fixtures.
+
+Primary browser acceptance fixture:
+
+`/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/qa/2026-11-23-north-xitun-continue/immutable-ordinary-v12-production/27-24-18-ordinary.sav`
+
+SHA-256: `fe8ceab2f84364342f440da4f9166e40a7b1845e5341bdf91175ca440ac7e8e9`.
+
+Expected: native `43:27`, local `[24,18]` → `[23,20]`, authored world `[63,80]` → `[62,82]`.
