+# North Xitun neighborhood implementation
+
+Implements the user's November 23 request to build the held North Xitun draft: Sakura Evening Market, unified Huimin Park, and the wider Xitun Civic Housing frontage. These are scenery and neighborhood points of interest. No gym, interior, street, tower, landmark entrance, NPC, map registration or map shape is added or moved; the existing ten gyms remain.
+
+Native baseline: `0e9363298301c83f0db7e7b1bf3d44d918be5b20`. Web reference for the existing overview/emulator: `4711be42fba47fedc9fc3b4a4c41f0d8def4f538`. Both release reference worktrees were read-only throughout. Work branch: `codex/north-xitun-neighborhoods`.
+
+## Authorship and placement
+
+The original preview is `north-of-taiwan-boulevard.html` in Executive Decisions' visualization folder. Its exported `placement-draft.json` and both original Python drawing commands are retained in `source/`. The commands were recovered from that chat's original tool records (`exec-cdca2c76-5cd3-4376-8190-e67f333b02b6`, followed by `exec-411d04b6-5891-41f8-84de-9cc8c43de447`). Implementation uses these authored coordinates and existing sprites, rather than inferring placements from pixels.
+
+| Area | Authored world rectangle, half-open | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Sakura Evening Market | `[55,76,70,89]` | Attached shops, produce carts, breakfast cart, tea umbrella and planted edge; Qinghai sidewalk/aisle stays connected |
+| Huimin Park | `[100,67,118,87]` | One walkable lawn, original eight path rectangles, shaded loop, four entrances, benches and sand play detail |
+| Xitun Civic Housing | `[98,92,109,104]` | Existing full-lot apartment sprite at its drafted size, planted forecourt and clear central approach beside Huizhong Park |
+
+`tools/taichung/boulevard_city/north-xitun.json` is the implementation's complete placement/ground blueprint. `north_xitun.py` applies it after the approved tower installation, removes only fully-contained old objects and verifies that new envelopes stay within these three blocks. Tree trunks use base collision and overhead canopies; carts/benches use the existing kit's authored base footprints. Decorative tufts/flowers and most of the sand remain walkable; the small wooden play fixture blocks its own two base cells.
+
+The sand/play PNG is generated from the draft's original drawing instructions. Its native colors reuse the existing street-furniture palette to fit the 64 virtual-palette limit. All other art remains the existing library's designs and proportions. The normal streamed-tileset palette conversion and stacking still apply.
+
+## Compiled and runtime evidence
+
+- The retained release authoring snapshot reproduced **all 340 original native outputs byte for byte** before this change.
+- Comparing **227,652 resolved map and camera-border cells**, all **559 changed world cells** are inside the three approved rectangles. All other pixels, metatile attributes and collision are identical to production. Shared numeric tile IDs change more widely because the global graphics pool is repacked.
+- All **54 maps**, **40,041 walkable cells** and **186 directed map connections** are reachable. Landmarks, capture signs, street people, warps, connections and the approved tower block match the production report exactly.
+- Every cell of the park's eight path rectangles and all four entrance anchors pass collision assertions.
+- Full native ROM build passed. A second generation reproduced all 340 installed/tested native outputs exactly.
+- Worst 17×17 camera window: **778/1,011 graphics slots**, **13/13 palette slots**. Metatiles: **1,552/2,048**. Global graphics pool: 14,967/65,536; virtual palettes remain within 64.
+
+Controller sweeps run the actual compiled cartridge in mGBA, using isolated relocated test saves and controller buttons. They do not move the player by writing RAM. Both walking and biking passed every case with zero failures:
+
+| Area | Accessible tiles per mode | Directed movement steps per mode | Solid-face probes per mode | Native maps crossed |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| Market | 345 | 1,178 | 72 | 27 ↔ 35 |
+| Park | 511 | 1,892 | 60 | 35 |
+| Housing | 335 | 1,184 | 41 | 35 ↔ 36 |
+
+The camera-border comparison covers all native maps and their nine-tile supplied borders; runtime routes cross the neighboring map seams in both modes. `source-validation.json` and `travel-summary.json` record the checks. Player views are unmodified native 240×160 emulator frames, without the browser HD overlay. Full-block images are native data renders enlarged with nearest-neighbor sampling.
+
+![North Xitun context](north-xitun-review.png)
+
+![Market block](sakura-evening-market-block.png)
+![Market player view](sakura-evening-market-player.png)
+
+![Huimin block](huimin-park-block.png)
+![Huimin player view](huimin-park-player.png)
+
+![Housing block](xitun-civic-housing-block.png)
+![Housing player view](xitun-civic-housing-player.png)
+
+## Rebuild and Main handoff
+
+The authoritative retained authoring inputs remain at `/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/qa/2026-11-23-combined-release/authoring`. `source-inputs.json` hashes all 147 retained input files and dependencies, including kit images and source geometry. The new blueprint/compiler and regenerated native data are in this commit. With Python/Pillow, from the native checkout:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/boulevard_city/compile_snapshot.py \
+  /path/to/this-native-checkout \
+  /path/to/2026-11-23-combined-release/authoring \
+  /tmp/north-xitun-output
+```
+
+This emits staged native data and `build-report.json`. Source-map QA needs Pillow and the primary tiles generated by the normal native build:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/boulevard_city/verify_north_xitun.py \
+  /path/to/this-native-checkout /path/to/qa-directory \
+  /path/to/production-native-city-overview.png
+```
+
+The QA directory contains `production-baseline/` and `candidate/` staged outputs. Retained outputs are under `/Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/qa/2026-11-23-north-xitun/`:
+
+- `candidate/build-report.json`: source hashes, new placements/collision footprints, unchanged map origins/connections, and updated walkability.
+- `candidate/city-overview.png`: updated 6-pixel-per-tile website/radar picture, with only the three approved block rectangles replaced in the production overview.
+- `north-xitun-destinations.json`: bilingual scenery IDs, local/native approach coordinates and website-space coordinates. Authored world x minus 31 equals the existing website/radar x; y is unchanged. These are game positions, not real GPS. Existing markers do not move.
+- `roms/`: local test cartridge and receipt. No ROM or save fixture is committed.
+- `*-travel.json`: detailed runtime results; `*-block.png` and `*-player.png`: independently reviewable visuals.
+
+Main should regenerate the HD pack against the assembled cartridge using the verified web `scripts/hd-world.py`; the existing original artwork for shops, apartments and props remains in the project asset library. The small code-drawn sand detail is native ground art and does not introduce a new high-resolution facade. Use the updated compiled report and overview for the website map/radar pairing. Map origins, road bands and existing landmark anchors are unchanged; preserve unrelated bilingual-label work. Main retains combined build, existing-save/Continue and stale map-cache checks, preview assembly and publication. This branch has not changed or published the website.
+
+The FamilyMart source audit is separate commit `7f7344eb2ce900feaa2272d96874975502eb0afa`: its HD artwork already exists. Interface owns the active-dialogue rendering investigation.
