diff --git a/docs/old-core-graphics-budget.md b/docs/old-core-graphics-budget.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e0bd8aa9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/old-core-graphics-budget.md
@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@
+# OldCity graphics feasibility audit
+
+A scene-specialized primary clone has enough graphics space for the currently
+encoded Station, Miyahara V2, Park and color kit in arithmetic. The explicit
+allowlist leaves 412 unused primary graphic indices. The combined pool requires
+668 new patterns after reuse of a preserved static primary pattern; 412 primary
+holes plus 376 usable secondary slots leave 120 raw slots unallocated.
+
+This is a read-only feasibility result. No clone, graphic assignment, metatile
+remapping or native map change has been created. Runtime correctness remains
+unproven. Exact input hashes, per-input metatile/graphic allowlists and pattern
+pool metadata are in `data/taichung/landmarks/old-core-bank-audit.json`.
+
+## Explicit preservation scope
+
+The raw primary reservation includes every General graphic referenced by:
+
+- All cells and borders of current `TaichungOldCity`, `TaichungGreenway` and
+  `TaichungXitun`, including primary-graphic references inside their secondary
+  metatile definitions.
+- Every module in the complete source prefab catalog.
+- The V4 64×64 filled fixture and its complete block catalog.
+- Every named `METATILE_General_*` definition, providing a conservative closure
+  for common General grass-cut and door replacements.
+- All 70 fixed graphics overwritten by `InitTilesetAnim_General`.
+
+| Primary reservation | Graphics |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Referenced raw indices, including named dynamic definitions | 166 |
+| Fixed animation indices | 70 |
+| Overlap between those sets | 8 |
+| Total reserved indices | 228 |
+| Unreferenced raw indices available to a new clone | 412 |
+
+The audit lists all 412 candidate indices explicitly. It does not move any used
+graphic or require source-entry changes for this raw-hole option. A compiler
+could copy General into a new local primary and replace only those unused slots.
+The global General source must stay unchanged. This scope does not cover other
+maps, future prefabs, new connections or arbitrary metatile replacements.
+
+The General callback writes 416..463, 464..481 and 508..511. These 70 destinations
+stay at their original indices and cannot hold static artwork. A static pattern
+must not share an animated destination merely because its initial frame matches.
+
+## Full-General reference
+
+Preserving every General definition by flip-aware repacking requires 517 static
+patterns plus the 70 fixed animation slots: 587 occupied primary slots and only
+53 free. That approach would also need every affected primary-graphic reference
+in General and secondary definitions remapped. Its available room is insufficient
+for the measured pool: the deficit after those 53 slots and usable secondary is
+239 graphics. The larger 412-hole result depends on the explicit scene allowlist.
+
+## Measured OldCity pools
+
+| Pool | Unique indexed patterns before cross-pool deduplication |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Station | 225 |
+| Miyahara V2 | 152 |
+| Park encoded candidate | 185 |
+| Complete source/color kit | 110 |
+
+The source/color kit is measured from the current complete catalog and recipe
+compiled in memory: 62 source patterns plus 48 colored patterns. Its pattern set
+matches the V4 native color fixture. This is the current recipe count; earlier
+prototype counts are not treated as an allocation. Actually referenced current
+OldCity secondary graphics are included in the union as an additional guard.
+
+All three landmark rasters use the exact same 16-entry Station palette7. The
+source kit retains its existing palette references and colored roofs use 12.
+Graphic deduplication compares indexed patterns including flips; the same index
+pattern can serve different palettes because palette selection belongs to the
+metatile reference. This audit does not merge RGB colors or change any palette.
+
+Station and Miyahara share one pattern. Their union is 376. With Park, the kit
+and current OldCity secondary references, the total union is 669. One pattern
+already exists in preserved nonanimated General graphics, leaving 668 patterns
+to place. The JSON records pool hashes and exact candidate paths.
+
+## Capacity and definition limits
+
+Secondary background graphics physically contain 384 slots. Door animation
+overwrites global graphics 1016..1023, leaving 376 slots for static artwork.
+Station's current bank has 289 unique graphics and 304 loaded sheet slots, so it
+has 87 raw unique slots or 72 slots after its present padding. Appending each
+landmark as a separate full bank is not a valid combined allocation.
+
+The specialized raw-hole option has 788 available slots across primary holes
+and usable secondary. Placing all 668 measured patterns would consume at least
+292 primary holes if secondary were filled to 376. At the other arithmetic end,
+using all 412 primary holes would leave 256 patterns for secondary. Neither is an
+implemented allocation. The 120 remaining slots are not a reserve for unmeasured
+features, and actual references must exclude door scratch even when a sheet has
+padding there.
+
+A separate envelope-only metatile estimate is 79 original secondary slots,
+96 Station cells, 80 Miyahara cells, 96 Park cells and 32 color variants: 383 of 384
+definitions. This is tight and may shrink by omitting empty or duplicate cells.
+Candidate/color IDs currently overlap and require rebasing. Layer attributes,
+background composition, old-ID preservation and actual allocation have not been
+compiled by this audit.
+
+## Dynamic and engine requirements
+
+The raw-hole count becomes usable only after the integrator constrains every
+runtime path that could reference an unpreserved General definition:
+
+- Grass cutting maps General grass/tree-top cells to mowed definitions. All
+  named General labels are included, but other tileset-specific cut mappings
+  require an explicit policy.
+- Scripted `setmetatile` accepts arbitrary IDs. No direct replacement command is
+  present in the scanned Taichung scripts, but transitive specials, future scripts
+  and saved map mutations still require review.
+- The ash effect restores a metatile from runtime arguments. PCs, special floors,
+  escalators and other map-specific animations also perform replacement. They
+  must be unreachable in these exteriors or added to the allowlist.
+- The clone must retain General's callback, all animation destinations, primary
+  palettes 0..6, IDs and attributes needed by allowed General/secondary definitions.
+  Unused General definitions can still reference reclaimed graphic indices and
+  are not safe merely because their numeric IDs remain present.
+- All General graphics used anywhere in the three current exteriors and borders
+  are reserved for connection previews. Neighbor secondary compatibility, map
+  reload/cache behavior, saves and future seams still need native verification.
+- Door animation owns its eight scratch graphics. Walking, cycling, animated
+  entry/returns, field effects and primary/secondary reloads need emulator checks.
+
+Primary field effects that use object sprites do not automatically establish
+background safety; argument-driven background replacement must be considered
+separately. The audit's `engineSafetyClaim` remains false.
+
+## Reproduction and provenance
+
+Run `tools/taichung/landmarks/audit_old_core_primary.py` with Pillow-enabled Python
+after generating the V4 fixture. The tool writes only its audit JSON. Two runs
+matched apart from the requested output path, all 76 input files stayed unchanged,
+and free indices are disjoint from every required graphic and animation slot.
+Park was encoded by the time this audit ran, so its 185 patterns and exact palette
+match are measured rather than estimated. Future dynamic reserves remain unknown.
+
+The separate Miyahara EOL audit is complete. Both candidate palette files already
+use CRLF, both encoders explicitly write CRLF and Git's `*.pal text eol=crlf`
+restores the same bytes at checkout. No RGB/PNG/study bytes changed and no V1
+preservation exception was needed. Both Miyahara format checkers still pass.
diff --git a/docs/old-core-native-checklist.md b/docs/old-core-native-checklist.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..be1a894b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/old-core-native-checklist.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Old-core native validation and runtime handoff
+
+`tools/taichung/landmarks/check_old_core.py` checks the actual compiled and
+installed shared bank. It reads the compiler manifest and native source bytes;
+it does not import the compiler, write maps, change C/registries, build a ROM or
+open an emulator. Its JSON result fingerprints the manifest and read source set.
+
+```sh
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/landmarks/check_old_core.py --json --self-test
+```
+
+The default inputs are the actual `old-core-native/manifest.json`, the immutable
+audit reference `a155d17`, and Main's opening reference `21c08cb`. Use `--source`,
+`--manifest`, `--audit-reference` and `--opening-reference` for an intentional
+contract revision. The validator prints to stdout only. Root can retain that
+output alongside the exact feature build and ROM hash.
+
+## Static gates
+
+| Gate | Concrete check |
+| --- | --- |
+| Global General stays original | Compare 40 tracked General files to the audit commit; compare the 10 exact working-tree hashes recorded by the audit, including palettes 0–6. Git-normalized text palettes also compare their line contents. |
+| Primary clone preserves live graphics | Compare all 228 protected raw graphic indices pixel-for-pixel, including all 70 fixed General animation destinations. Preserve palettes 0–6, General metatile IDs, the 86 allowed definitions/attributes and the General callback. |
+| Actual bank and C bindings | Resolve C tiles, palettes, metatiles and attribute declarations to the validated bank paths. Check actual sheet/definition capacities, valid layer types, palette indices and every used static graphic reference below 1016. New static art must not reuse a General animation destination. |
+| Shared palette | Compare palette 7 to the exact approved Station palette and both Miyahara V2/Park source rasters. Compare source/color metatiles to the frozen native-color fixture, including palette 12. |
+| Preserved source appearance | Compare rendered pixels and full attributes for the three districts' required General/Pewter IDs, both complete source catalogs and V4 color/infill inputs. |
+| Actual landmark artwork | Decode the real bank's foreground quadrants and compare them to the three approved indexed rasters, including flips and palette selection. Verify roof/front layer attributes, collision words, occupied map cells and the functional General door words. |
+| Stable routes and returns | Use actual source attributes, map collision and elevations for BFS, district connections and all ten gym bindings. The three changed landmarks retain their original door, approach, arrival and three interior return bindings. Reject unpaired active OldCity doors. |
+| Connection previews | Require all three districts to use the compatible shared bank cohort. Compare the actual borrowed connection strips under the viewer's bank, including the engine's 8-column east strip. |
+| Other district preservation | Greenway/Xitun map and border words remain identical to `21c08cb`; compare their rendered RGB and attributes under the new bank. |
+| Current dynamic roots | Resolve all named General C labels/macros and current Taichung script replacements against the protected/defined namespace. Reject an unprotected General ID or a new exterior behavior outside the audited set. |
+| Welcome flow remains Main's | Compare the guide object, transition/resume/frame scripts, graphical-selector hooks, C welcome guards and spawn to `21c08cb`. Preserve map group numbers, welcome group 43/number 13, 65 walkable cells after the guide, clear spawn/front and the direct outdoor anchor. |
+
+The first independent run found 16 colored-metatile preview mismatches: Greenway
+could borrow OldCity's new frontage words while still using its old secondary
+bank. Root corrected the actual layouts to the shared cohort. The repeated check
+then compared 1,530 borrowed strip cells with zero mismatches and confirmed all
+5,448 Greenway/Xitun map/border words and their appearance were unchanged.
+
+The checked bank contains 258 unique secondary graphics, 272 loaded slots and
+299 secondary definitions. The run also compared 1,038 source/catalog/V4
+metatiles, 188 landmark foreground cells, all ten gym bindings, 24 walkable seam
+crossings and 4,871 reachable exterior nodes. These describe the checked source
+snapshot; later compiler changes require another run. The report records actual
+source hashes instead of treating this paragraph as a permanent build claim.
+
+`--self-test` changes private in-memory copies to verify detection of a protected
+graphic corruption, a door-scratch reference and a layer-bit corruption. It
+does not create a second bank or mutate the real files.
+
+Installed infill without a placement manifest still receives actual-ID, native
+attribute, source-color and route checks. The checker does not claim a complete
+prefab paint/mandatory-clear-mask placement proof without those placement inputs.
+Argument-driven engine handlers and saved-map restoration remain explicit
+runtime/review limits; resolving named C roots is not a universal engine-safety
+claim.
+
+## Root's isolated runtime pass
+
+Root owns the feature build and computer-use QA. Use the existing
+`tools/taichung/qa_server.py` with an explicit feature ROM, an mGBA runtime folder
+and an unused local port. Its arguments are `--rom`, `--runtime` and `--port`.
+No canonical ROM or server on port 4184 is part of this validation workstream.
+The server already supplies the required COOP/COEP headers and `no-store`.
+
+The existing `qa.html` harness supports a fresh unique save by default and a
+stable `?qaSave=<token>` for controlled Continue checks. Reload the tab and load
+the rebuilt feature cartridge after a ROM rebuild; an emulator already running
+keeps its old cartridge bytes. Record the exact source/ROM hash and save token.
+
+1. Start a fresh feature save. Confirm the welcome guide and frame-driven
+   introduction appear inside the room, finish a real starter selection and
+   reach OldCity `(30,66)` with controls restored. Check a language switch with
+   actual native text. Source binding parity is already checked; this verifies
+   loading the new outdoor bank during the transition.
+2. Walk and cycle past the Station, Miyahara and Park. Inspect each silhouette
+   and roof/front layering from the south, east and west. Wait long enough to
+   see General water/flower animation; watch for overwritten or flickering
+   landmark/roof graphics.
+3. Enter all three changed gyms through their real doors and return. Inspect
+   the door-opening frames and stable approach/arrival positions. The door
+   animation uses graphics 1016–1023, which static artwork must never reference.
+4. Cross OldCity–Greenway and Greenway–Xitun in both directions. Pause before
+   crossing so borrowed edge previews are visible; recheck after crossing and
+   returning. Verify unchanged neighborhood pixels, palette reloads and walking
+   or cycling control at the seams.
+5. Save/Continue on the isolated feature save near each changed landmark and
+   after a seam crossing. Separately test a save created before this retile;
+   keep that result distinct from a fresh post-retile save. Capture the actual
+   game canvas using the harness's screen-download control, which rejects an
+   all-black capture. A source renderer image is not runtime evidence.
+
+The checker itself does not start a server, use a browser, inspect the canonical
+ROM or mark any of these runtime steps passed.
+
+## Main-owned cache compatibility decision
+
+The map group and existing door IDs stay stable, but the OldCity geometry and
+new secondary metatile meanings have changed. A pre-retile save may restore old
+viewport words over a newly loaded map even when its saved player position is
+valid. Root's bank check cannot establish that Continue invalidates or migrates
+that cache.
+
+Main owns the cache/version migration decision and its verification. This
+workstream flags the need, records `verifiedWithPreRetileContinue=false`, and adds
+no cache hook, save-version allocation or startup rewrite. A successful fresh
+new-game route is not evidence that a pre-retile Continue is compatible.
