+# Optional Story adapter: all20 existing places
+
+Based on live native586b8a84 and the first four-place checkpointb8ca7c49.
+The manifest pins all20 existing-place JSON packages to committed frontend
+bdde783a0ee7077918b09b713150903eee2b46a1. The first four package bytes are
+unchanged. No future-place package, moving checkout content, network source,
+new object, geometry, art, saved field or capture allocation is imported.
+
+## Player-visible behavior
+
+All20 existing signs show the package's actual English or Traditional Chinese
+short sign, always one page with at most two lines. Long history and attributed
+staff notes open only after an explicit choice. Each sign retains MSGBOX_SIGN;
+public script labels and the actual map objects remain unchanged.
+
+All ten gym leaders keep their original short question and native challenge
+path. Challenge is index0; About, Staff notes, Back and B do not prepare battles.
+Reading returns to the same original question. Completed leaders retain optional
+reading without permitting rematches or awards. First-victory award flow is intact.
+
+The nine currently bound capture signs and Wenchang's interior host offer
+Encounter / About / Staff / Back. Explicit Encounter enters the existing native
+wrapper and its original Prepare / Begin / Later protocol. No persistence,
+party, encounter, save or battle operation is implemented in this adapter.
+Reading/Back/B/replay never enters the capture protocol. Optional reading is
+available regardless of whether an attempt is spent or already unlocked.
+
+Wenchang's exterior sign remains informational. Wanhe's information host remains
+informational. The existing eight other sight signs and Maple sign retain their
+original0–9 encounter assignments; sites10–13 and Tiger City are not activated.
+
+All five original named NPCs and five helper objects are preserved. Their exact
+entry labels select the correct place, before and after victory. Notes are
+voluntary; Qiaoqiao retains separate Research and Garden notebooks. An explicit
+attribution identifies worker notes when accessed from a leader, sign or host,
+so first-person worker statements do not become leader speech.
+
+## Three separate ID namespaces
+
+| Place | Story text ID | Gym/save bit | Capture site |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+|Station/Park/Miyahara/Science/Greenway/ShenJi/FineArts/Fengjia|0–7|0–7|None|
+|Maple Garden|8|None|0|
+|Theater|9|9|None|
+|Wenchang Temple|10|None|1, interior host only|
+|Wanhe Temple / Muqing|11|8|None|
+|Botanical/Confucius/Yizhong/Prefectural/SecondMarket/Heritage/Fengle/Wenxin|12–19|None|2–9|
+
+These relationships are explicit in the source manifest, C data and independent
+host-test roster. History IDs0–11 retain their meanings;12–19 are new text-only
+keys. The old12-entry history table/count are unchanged. No gym mask, capture
+mask, map ID or save version is extended.
+
+VAR_0x8006 is the selected temporary text key. VAR_0x8004 remains the original gym
+ID during Challenge and becomes a site ID only inside an existing capture
+wrapper. Thus Muqing's gym8 selects Wanhe text11 while preparation still sees8;
+Maple's sign/helper selects text8 and only its explicit action routes to site0.
+Informational selection and leader selection are separate C APIs. A formatter
+will not restore a question for a mismatched gym/text cohort.
+
+## Source and regeneration
+
+- `data/taichung/optional-story/manifest.json` pins exactly20 copied packages,
+  source hashes, stable text IDs, original sign labels and explicit action cohorts.
+- `render-optional-story.py` validates source hashes, fact/source references,
+  bilingual page/line bounds and encoded buffer bounds. It emits only the new
+  optional C table and generated sign-wrapper include. It never changes the old
+  history C/data, source packages, glyphs, maps or source locks.
+- `taichung_optional_story.c` selects immutable text and restores the original
+  read-only question formatter. Only text buffers, VAR_RESULT and the temporary
+  text selector are written. There is no new RAM allocation or saved state.
+- Existing city signs/temple hosts redirect to the adapter. Existing worker
+  scripts keep their objects, replay guards and lock/release lifecycle.
+- Menus70–73 remain intact;74 adds the localized Encounter/reading menu. All old
+  native menu IDs and the old67 Challenge/Leave list remain unchanged.
+
+From this native checkout:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/render-optional-story.py --write
+python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/render-optional-story.py
+bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-optional-story.sh
+```
+
+Generation is idempotent. There are150 content pages per language, at most two
+lines per page, maximum198px line width and each encoded message below the native
+1000-byte buffer budget. UI labels and worker credits are audited too. Individual
+signs are constrained to one page before the reading choice.
+
+## Verification
+
+Actual new C compiles in GNU89 with declaration-after-statement errors enabled.
+Its1050 combinations cover both languages, mixed gym masks including only bit8,
+all14 capture bits/reserved-bit examples and virgin/known/partial/future capture
+namespaces. Opaque full-save/identity/options/storage sentinels remain unchanged.
+Independent expected leader/site cohorts exercise the Maple/Wanhe distinction.
+
+The actual-script interpreter checks4620 paths over a fixed42-entry roster:
+20 signs,10 leaders,10 workers and2 temple hosts. It also verifies the actual map
+objects still reference each original entry once. Each selected/displayed place
+is checked independently of the generated manifest. Direct actions, optional
+reading, Back/B, replay, completed gyms and spent-state inputs are covered.
+At an explicit capture action it verifies the correct original wrapper/site and
+stops at native Offer; it does not fabricate a battle, ACK, result or win.
+
+Twelve disposable mutations must fail, including Park worker reading Miyahara,
+a native Park actor pointing at Miyahara, Maple sign reading Wanhe, gym8/Wanhe11
+cohort corruption, Wenchang exterior capture activation, a sign entering future
+site10, required long history, Back starting action, wrong Qiaoqiao topic and
+capture-mask clearing in actual C. No real map or SRAM bytes are mutated.
+
+## Glyphs
+
+Use only the existing pinned append pipeline:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/extend-chinese-glyphs.py --artifacts /tmp/story-all20-glyph-review
+python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/extend-chinese-glyphs.py --artifacts /tmp/story-all20-glyph-review --write
+```
+
+The all20 addition needs166 glyphs after the857 first-slice prefix: indices
+857–1022, final1023. All857 previous encoded indices/bitmap rows, including every
+808 released glyph, remain byte-exact. The current pinned Fusion Pixel12px zh_tw
+source and licenses are unchanged. Do not run a sorting/reset generator.
+
+## Remaining integration and runtime acceptance
+
+No full ROM, emulator, deployment or corrected-city approval is claimed here.
+Main must add exact registered Story qualification above the existing strict
+source guards, preserving every historical profile/probe and validating current
+inputs before any baseline substitution. Legacy history tests retain their
+original baseline behavior; this adapter does not weaken them to claim a raw pass.
+
+After an authorized combined ROM/ELF build, check actual EN/ZH signs, all original
+workers and optional menus, direct Challenge/Encounter, Back/B, post-win/spent
+reading, both Qiaoqiao topics, Maple text8/site0 versus Muqing gym8/Wanhe11, and the
+Wenchang sign/host separation. Verify genuine native Save/Continue preserves
+party, capture tuples and preferences. Field capture durability remains owned by
+the unchanged native protocol and its Main runtime acceptance.
