+# Production encounter follow-up —23 November2026
+
+Base native0e9363298301c83f0db7e7b1bf3d44d918be5b20. Existing production geometry,
+21stable saved IDs (17currently available), EC02 schema, three scoped Ultra Balls
+and the72-byte v2 bridge are the baseline. One attempt per save remains unchanged.
+
+## Silent Begin and explicit breakouts
+
+Begin closes the offer and starts the existing save/wait path without a routine
+"Saving this attempt" message. Failure to prepare or begin still takes the error
+message path. Native flash, matching save generation/masks and browser durable ACK
+still precede battle; storage failure still uses the existing actionable message.
+
+The vanilla one-shake escape line was "It appeared to be caught!". It is a failed
+ball result, not a capture result. All four failed-shake presentation variants now
+dispatch the same explicit English/Traditional Chinese failure sentence. The actual
+ball RNG, catch formula, shakes, animation and success script are unchanged.
+Failure scripts do not execute `givecaughtmon`. Only the true scoped catch script
+executes that command; the core additionally requires matching capture provenance
+before a caught outcome can grant the unlock. An actual-C Snorlax regression spends
+a ball without capture provenance and confirms even a false caught outcome grants
+no unlock. Knockout/run/loss/exhaustion/interruption retain the consumed attempt.
+
+Checks: `test-playtest-messages.py`, `test-encounter.sh`,
+`test-encounter-field.sh` under `tools/taichung_gameplay`. The text test executes
+the actual dispatch/getter in both languages and reads the actual battle/field
+scripts. Native field/core tests preserve the durable barrier and unsuccessful/
+caught paths. These are source/host checks; Main owns combined cartridge/browser QA.
+
+## Explicit menu and battle return
+
+Prepare stores its encounter site outside temporary script variables, then
+returns through a dedicated native field callback to `OfferPrepared`. The
+prepared party remains in the ordinary native team store. The offer is shown
+again directly and selects Begin by default; the initial offer still selects
+Prepare. Preparing or backing out never consumes an attempt.
+
+The scoped battle-end callback now returns through
+`TaichungEncounterReturnToField`. Once the live map is rebuilt, it starts the
+normal native save preflight while the field fade runs. This removes the old
+wait for the full return fade before beginning the outcome commit. Native flash
+and the matching browser durable ACK are still required. The result script starts
+explicitly only after both ACK and fade completion, in either arrival order.
+No bridge version, offsets, masks, sequence or ACK semantics changed. The obsolete
+script-side `TaichungEncounter_ScriptSaveResult` call is removed.
+
+A true confirmed catch immediately displays the existing Add to team question.
+Full parties proceed to the existing party picker and replacement confirmation;
+its selected slot and site are retained across field reload too. Cancel leaves
+the durable unlock available in Team. Append/replacement use the existing native
+team API and the site's captured level, not the ordinary level-50 default.
+Existing party members remain usable if their species has no new unlock.
+The outcome save durably records the attempt and catch before this optional
+party editing. Subsequent party changes use the game's normal save behavior.
+
+Storage failure at Begin or result still opens the actionable backup/continue
+message. It cannot display the Add offer or start another battle. Every consumed
+noncapture outcome keeps its attempt bit without granting an unlock.
+
+`test-encounter-field.sh` now runs the real core/bridge/field C plus the actual
+scripted-wild battle-end callback. Checks include all 17 active Prepare returns,
+preserved prepared parties, both return fade/ACK orders, native/browser result
+save failures, true-catch add/replace, selection preservation, and every consumed
+noncapture result. It also links real encounter and team C together for all 17
+captured levels, append/replace, legacy existing-party usability and native save
+variable restoration after catch and knockout. Engine/GBA services and saved
+snapshots are modeled; combined cartridge persistence is Main's verification.
+
+## Interface status contract
+
+No bridge ABI change in this slice. Use the current v2 packet (72bytes), not old
+compact-candidate14-ID/64-byte assumptions. `attempts` and `unlocks` are flattened
+u32 masks at offsets0x20/0x24; `site`0x2A, `phase`0x2B, `balls`0x2C,
+`result`0x2D, `saveStatus`0x2E. Available profiles exclude the retired IDs.
+
+Per available site, an attempt bit with no unlock is consumed without a catch;
+refresh/Continue after an interrupted durable Begin must preserve that marker.
+An unlock bit represents a genuine catch. For the packet's current site, pending
+phases1–4 should be shown as in-progress rather than a new available attempt or a
+final durable catch. Phase6/storage error needs recovery presentation; pending
+RAM unlocks are not a substitute for the result ACK. Phase5 follows matching
+durability; on a validated restored native save, masks remain authoritative even
+with transient phase0. Interface owns rendering these states.
