index 00000000..22de0b1c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/taichung-badge-bridge.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Read-only native badge scene
+
+`gTaichungBadgeBridge` is a separate 32-byte v1 mailbox (`TCBDG001`). It does
+not change the capture v2/72-byte packet, EC02 save schema, gym bits or native
+award/input flow. Main should emit `badgeBridge` metadata with the matching
+ELF address, version1, size32, magicA0x44424354 and magicB0x31303047, and re-pin
+the existing bridge addresses from that same ELF.
+
+| Offset | Type | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 00/04 | u32/u32 | Magic A/B |
+| 08/0A | u16/u16 | Version1 / size32 |
+| 0C | u32 | Native self address |
+| 10 | u32 | Publication: odd during write, stable nonzero even afterward |
+| 14 | u32 | Frame counter, advances when native game callbacks ran |
+| 18 | u16 | Completed gym mask, bits0–9 |
+| 1A | u8 | Scene0none / 1collection / 2award |
+| 1B | u8 | Native selected gym0–9, or255 outside a badge scene |
+| 1C | u8 | Flags: bit0visible; other bits0 |
+| 1D | u8 | Native scene language1EN / 2ZH, or0 outside |
+| 1E | u16 | Reserved0 |
+
+The browser owns no packet bytes. It must require a unique advancing packet,
+stable publication, correct metadata/reserved values and visible bit before
+rendering. Native selection and packet language are authoritative. Native retains
+all buttons, fanfare, dismissal, collection navigation and trainer-card behavior.
+There is no browser request, ACK, progress write or award trigger.
+
+The getter checks the actual native City Pass callback and active input task.
+Opening/closing, palette fades, skipped callbacks, battle and replay hide the
+overlay; the Trainer Card detour and all other callbacks publish scene0. Closing
+is hidden immediately, including the final fade frame, to avoid an extra overlay
+flash. Window/resource failures cannot leave a stale scene. Outside a badge
+scene the completed mask/language are0 and selectedGym is255; the existing
+navigation bridge supplies ordinary field progress.
+
+Scene2 describes an award screen that native already authorized and opened.
+Never infer a new award from a mask change. Old completion masks render only
+the collection and do not create reward events. The future Confucius/Rites swap
+retains selectedGym5 and completed bit32.
+
+`test-badge-scenes.sh` runs actual native scene, progress, award adapters and
+mailbox C. It covers both languages/all1024 old masks, every new award, selection,
+trainer-card return, early/held dismissal, replay, allocation failures, hidden
+states and publication rollover. No new persistent state is allocated; the sole
+packet uses32 bytes of EWRAM.
