@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Taichung battle AI
+
+The live baseline a701ed51 gives all ten city leaders only
+`AI_SCRIPT_CHECK_BAD_MOVE` (1). Scripted landmark encounters also use that flag.
+All moves start at 100. The native bad-move script only discourages a pure defense
+increase at the stat cap12; below that it can remain tied with an attack. The
+native selector chooses randomly among its highest scores. Its existing choice
+and RNG algorithm are preserved.
+
+The ten registered leaders now use bad-move checking, viability and finishing:
+`AI_SCRIPT_CHECK_BAD_MOVE | AI_SCRIPT_CHECK_VIABILITY | AI_SCRIPT_TRY_TO_FAINT`
+(7). These existing FireRed scripts can encourage appropriate setup and give a
+feasible finishing attack+4. Street trainers and scripted-wild flags are unchanged.
+Landmarks retain their three-ball catch difficulty rather than gaining the
+leaders' full finishing policy.
+
+Flags alone do not fix Defense Curl: the native viability dispatch has no
+`EFFECT_DEFENSE_CURL` entry. After native scoring, a small Taichung-only policy
+subtracts8 from pure Defense/Sp.Def boosts once that defense is already+2
+(native stage8). This covers Defense Curl, Defense/Sp.Def up and their two-stage
+versions. An equally scored attack then beats another pure boost. Initial setup,
+Calm Mind/Bulk Up and other mixed offensive setup are untouched. The penalty is
+a preference, not a forced attack: if attacks have substantially worse scores,
+defense can still win. Zero-score/no-PP moves are not revived.
+
+Scope is a matching prepared and actually started registered gym challenge, or
+an active scoped landmark encounter. Other trainers, ordinary wild battles,
+untracked scripted wilds, and special flee/watch actions retain their behavior.
+No capture formula, ball RNG, one-attempt state, HP/PP recovery or trainer reward
+rule is changed. The policy adds no save fields or persistent RAM state.
+
+## Evidence
+
+`python3 -B tools/taichung_gameplay/test-battle-ai.py` compiles production policy,
+real move data, native RNG and the actual native selector, alongside a baseline
+selector with only the new call removed. It tests the scored-turn boundary;
+the complete AI bytecode VM and damage simulation are not replaced or claimed
+as executed by this host test. Representative native-script score outputs feed
+meaningful initial setup, a finishing attack, and spent pure-defense setup.
+
+- 4096 RNG seeds reproduce 1033 consecutive baseline defense selections at +2.
+  The scoped policy selects an equal-score attack in all 4096 corresponding turns.
+- Initial defense setup remains selectable in 2046 seeds; useful setup scored 102
+  and a finishing attack scored 104 keep their expected priority.
+- Mixed boosts, genuinely inferior attacks, no-PP/zero-score moves, outside-scope
+  trainers/wilds and flee/watch bypasses are covered.
+- The harness reads the actual bad-move cap, viability dispatch and finishing+4
+  script contract and checks all ten leader profiles and unchanged street/wild
+  flags.
+
+The modified cartridge compiles with the native agbcc toolchain. Its build log
+is `build/taichung-tests/ai/native-build.log`. Main owns combined battle acceptance.
