+# Twenty-four stable encounter slots
+
+The EC02 save layout is unchanged: vars40F4/40F5 contain the original low10
+attempt/caught bits (their high6 reserved bits stay untouched); vars40F0/40F2
+contain the upper16. Bit21/22/23 therefore use upper-word bits11/12/13.
+The supported mask is now00FFFFFF, with the same26-bit physical capacity.
+There is no new save variable, version or migration. Capture packet remains
+v2/72bytes, including32-bit masks, exact-save counter and durable ACK guards.
+Main must pair the browser's24-site registry/mask/proof bound with this ROM.
+
+All21 historical/retired identities retain their bits/species/levels/moves.
+Only site3's place changes: AlakazamLv65 moves from Confucius Temple to Shen Ji,
+using the same saved attempted/caught bit3. No new attempt is granted on old
+saves. Retired IDs2/8/9/15 stay reserved. New first-150 sites are:
+
+| Stable ID | Place / slug | Species | Captured level | Upper-word bit |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+|21|National Trade Center / national-trade-center|Magneton|65|11|
+|22|Ding Sheng BHW / ding-sheng-bhw|Kabutops|65|12|
+|23|The Lin / the-lin|Persian|65|13|
+
+The same one attempt and3Ultra Balls apply, with unchanged native catch odds
+and minimum catch rate45. These authored moves avoid recoil, flee/self-KO,
+healing or trapping effects; native AI and player battle controls remain.
+An attempted-only bit always means spent without a confirmed catch. Caught
+requires native capture recording plus matching caught outcome; breakout,
+KO, loss, run, exhaustion and interruption never unlock Team. Begin and
+result both require the matching complete native durable save/ACK. Preparing
+or viewing an offer never spends an attempt. Actual captured selections useLv65.
+
+Magneton, Kabutops and Persian were freely selectable before these new sites.
+Automatic party-level/preset maintenance now leaves all existing partners of
+these species untouched, regardless of available/spent/caught state. This
+preserves their exact saved level/EXP, identity, held item/mail, moves/PP/PP-Ups,
+HP/status/fainting without granting the capture unlock. New append/replacement
+selections remain locked until a true catch, and are created with normal
+presets at the captured level. Full healing after a valid gym victory still
+honors the existing On/Off preference, and ordinary blackout still recovers.
+
+Maps supplies the three TaichungLandmark_* thin dispatch labels and relocation
+of the Shen Ji interaction. This slice supplies registered TaichungEncounter_*
+wrappers and a legacy ConfuciusTemple symbol alias for still-linked archived
+scripts. No map geometry, Continue-cell table or Story dialogue is edited.
+No IDs24-26 or additional landmark pins/copy are allocated.
+
+Checks use real compiled encounter, bridge, field, team and save C:20active
+sites, durable-begin/result ACK ordering, all consumed outcomes, append/replace,
+Continue-reset/no retry, all three new upper bits, old Alakazam bit3, and exact
+existing rare-party bytes atLv5/50/80 in all3progress states. Existing-save
+regression covers70496 cases against the frozen save baseline. Registry audit
+compares all21 prior profiles to a701ed51 (only site3's slug changes), unchanged
+EC02/v2/72, original150 and safe moves. Full map-binding audit and actual ROM
+battle/flash acceptance run after Maps/Story/Main's combined source assembly;
+compiled host saves are distinguished from native SRAM exports.
+
+Historical upper-bit audit (`test-encounter-upper-history.py`): EC02 first
+appeared in3b8f0891, with count21; b5bab264 changes only Dragonite's place,
+and a701ed51 retains that core. All native/script references to upper vars
+are confined to the constants, encounter core, and read-only startup checks.
+Old initialization writes both complete upper words to0 before publishing
+EC02, including EC01 imports with arbitrary stale upper words. The only
+subsequent writes are `Saved(upper) | (1u << (site - 10))` from guarded Begin
+and confirmed capture; count21 bounds `site` to0..20, hence shifts0..10.
+By induction every released native-produced EC02 save has upper bits11..15
+zero. This proves newly supported21..23 start available without repurposing
+old progress. No schema change or sanitization is needed or performed.
+
+The102400-case differential check compiles the frozen actual a701ed51 core
+with its own frozen21-site header alongside the new core. It exercises all
+65536 EC01 stale-word patterns and all2048 historically reachable EC02 upper
+patterns through every old site's Begin/caught/KO writer, preserves reserved
+low bits, and compares old/new masks exactly. New-site bits remain0 throughout.
+An externally edited EC02 file with fabricated upper bits is outside that
+native provenance proof: with the deliberately unchanged schema it cannot be
+distinguished from legitimate new24-site progress. Clearing those bits on
+Continue would destroy genuine new saves, so no such destructive repair exists.
