+# Taichung native map handoff — 7 November 2026
+
+The compressed city blockout is committed and traversable in the actual FireRed
+ROM. Main owns integrating this branch with gameplay/localization and publishing.
+No canonical source checkout, web player, canonical ROM, or release patch was
+changed by this workstream.
+
+## Commits and native interface
+
+The branch is based on `ee75ad0` in `.worktrees/game-mapping`.
+
+- `50b6469`: generic source metatile/map renderer.
+- `b177182`: native collision, connection, arrival and paired-warp validator.
+- `8619822`: three connected outdoor districts, ten landmark lobbies, initial
+  blockout geometry/events, machine-readable mapping contract, region-map safety.
+- `0e1248f`: **separate one-line new-game spawn change**, Old city (30,66).
+- `34b1305`: named appended sections resolve after the stable NONE sentinel.
+- `684b253`, `955c5dc`, `8933227`: isolated browser QA harness and evidence capture.
+- `a23fdde`: reproducible stitched source overview and station close-up renderer.
+
+All actual game-code changes are present by `34b1305`; subsequent changes are QA,
+rendering and handoff tools/docs. Main can integrate the branch/ordered commits,
+keeping the spawn commit distinct for review.
+
+Native group43 contains Old city0, Greenway1, Xitun2 and the ten interiors3–12.
+`docs/taichung-city-contract.json` contains every stable landmark ID, room ID,
+exterior door/warp index, paired returns, sign, host, safe transport arrival and
+habitat reserve. `docs/taichung-mapping.md` explains topology and ownership.
+
+Original map/group/layout IDs and all original named region sections retain their
+values. `MAPSEC_NONE` remains197; new Taichung sections are198–200. The Sevii
+region search is bounded and `GetMapName` handles the appended names safely.
+
+## Build and static geometry proof
+
+Bootstrap and the selected-worktree build succeeded. Tested ROM:
+
+- 16,777,216 bytes.
+- SHA-1: `051893077c06f7159355a424abd2b85674db80ea`.
+- SHA-256: `1c35fb9f77dfc27ebebd67a4493f3aa813a784a8a66fb7e32da59c72e343222b`.
+- Isolated output: `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/roms/taichung-firered.gba`.
+
+`python3 tools/taichung/validate_city.py --baseline ee75ad0` passes:
+
+| District | Reachable outdoor cells from station |
+| --- | --- |
+| Old city | 1,785 |
+| Greenway | 1,927 |
+| Xitun | 1,549 |
+
+Every landmark approach, safe arrival, sign, host interaction space and all ten
+interior/return pairs pass static walking checks. There are24 directed open seam
+cells. Other boundary cells are closed; virtual-map capacity and real metatile
+behavior/collision/elevation are checked. Seven intentional in-memory fault probes
+were rejected, including bad doors, blocked approaches, broken seams and returns.
+
+## Actual emulator checks
+
+QA used the existing mGBA2.6.0 WebAssembly runtime in the separate local harness
+`tools/taichung/qa.html`, served by `qa_server.py`. Snapshot restoration was disabled
+and testing began with fresh native saves. Timed movement used the harness buttons;
+no debug warps or position patches were used.
+
+Observed in the running ROM:
+
+1. New game appears at the station plaza, language choice first, then a short
+   welcome and all four native starter choices. Pikachu was selected on one fresh
+   run; Charmander on a second. Bike and Save are immediately available.
+2. The station's animated door enters its actual lobby and returns to its own
+   exterior. Bike is rejected indoors; movement and outdoor cycling work afterward.
+3. Rode Old city → Greenway using the lower street, Greenway → Xitun, then
+   Xitun → Greenway and Greenway → Old city using the upper street. Both directions
+   of both district connections work; the two old-city roads form a usable loop.
+4. Entered the theater lobby from the bike, returned to the correct theater plaza,
+   and saved exactly at its contract arrival (12,47), map43,2.
+5. Save/Continue restored the Greenway location and bicycle. A full browser reload
+   also found and loaded the persisted native save at the theater. Starter and
+   language choices were not repeated.
+6. The park shoreline blocks walking/cycling into water. Native district banners
+   and Save headers show OLD TAICHUNG / TAICHUNG GREENWAY / TAICHUNG XITUN.
+
+Native save checkpoints (main fresh Charmander run):
+
+| Save counter | Native map | Position | Party |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | (43,0) Old city | (2,67) | 1 |
+| 2 | (43,1) Greenway | (22,68) | 1 |
+| 3 | (43,2) Xitun, theater arrival | (12,47) | 1 |
+| 4 | (43,0) Old city, park shore | (22,20) | 1 |
+
+The exported final save was parsed independently: language `VAR_0x40FB=1`, starter
+`VAR_0x40FC=4` (Charmander), optional tea state `VAR_0x40FD=1`, party count1. The
+valid fallback healer remains Pallet map(3,0), as documented for Main's replacement.
+
+Only station and theater doors were exercised manually; all ten door/return pairs
+are covered statically. This is not a claim of ten manually completed gym battles.
+
+## Review artifacts
+
+All outputs are outside the source checkout, under the isolated namespace:
