+# Native navigation and bike checkpoint
+
+Bike source is a separate commit from navigation. The native packet is an
+independent 48-byte, read-only version 1; the existing 32-byte language bridge
+is unchanged. `src/main.c` calls `TaichungNavigationBridge_Tick` once per main
+loop after game callbacks, immediately beside the language Tick.
+
+## Actual native evidence
+
+The corrected feature ROM tested here has SHA-1
+`7c0372426b1974cafd1a82105c05dd4f7d722cc2`, SHA-256
+`82560625274c1289ead7ef50d3ac2fb4d0fe74caa627b58cbc90b95453934a47`.
+It was loaded in a fresh runtime with snapshots disabled, then resumed through
+native Continue. The real Pikachu starter and Old City saved position `(35,66)`
+were retained, with no repeated opening.
+
+The private QA reader inspected the actual shared runtime heap. It required
+the matching native symbol address `0x0203F4AC`, coherent header/seqlock, and
+advancing sequence/frame counters over a 120ms probe. This address belongs to
+the tested feature ROM only; Main must derive the final canonical address.
+
+- Native walking moved to `(34,66)`, facing west. Packet: group 43/map 0,
+  width 40/height 72, flags 79 (READY/FIELD/POSITION_VALID/OUTDOOR/
+  CAN_TOGGLE_BIKE), context 0, sequence 12370/frame 6185.
+- A 1.2-second B hold mounted once. Subsequent cycling moved to `(30,66)` and
+  stopped before the adjacent sign. Packet: flags 111 (adds CYCLING), context
+  0, sequence 19252/frame 9626. Positions remained valid after ordinary motion.
+- A fresh B press dismounted. Packet retained `(30,66)`, flags 79, context 0,
+  sequence 23102/frame 11551. Field/menu controls remained usable.
+- Opening the native Start menu suspended the live position: flags 3,
+  context 16 (controls/script lock), coordinates -1/-1, map 255/255. Sequence
+  25490/frame 12745 still advanced. The browser must hide/suspend the minimap.
+- The graphical selector independently showed hidden context 18
+  (NOT_FIELD/SCRIPT), invalid coordinates and no bike eligibility.
+
+Runtime exposed that FireRed clears `CONTROLLABLE` during ordinary motion.
+The final publisher correctly validates active player + concrete locomotion
+state instead. Regression tests cover moving and stopped snapshots with that
+bit clear for walking, both bikes, surfing and underwater states.
+
+Strict host checks pass for actual navigation publication, structure offsets,
+bounds, all hidden contexts, eligibility flags, reserved zeros, stationary
+freshness and nonzero sequence/frame wrap. The actual bike-function checks
+cover fresh/held/modal/stale input, input priorities, short midstep queue,
+context/terrain/task limits, collisions and speed selection.
+
+## Integration and limits
+
+The schema/flags/units and rejection rules are in
+`taichung-navigation-bridge.md`. Publish canonical metadata with symbol address,
+version 1, size 48 and the two magic words only after the merged ROM is built.
+Minimap preference/rendering/persistence and map transforms remain with
+Interface/Mapping. No requests, party writes or saved-variable allocation are
+introduced by this packet.
+
+## Measured four-frame fallback
+
+The same native loss fixture was imported into two fresh isolated runtimes,
+then resumed through actual Continue and mounted with B. Its SHA-256 is
+`b74d59aba99efab0cc5a68ef3cce376d8ec697ab69c450604046deef7b381654`.
+Both measured Old City 43/0 `(30,66)` to `(34,66)` eastward. Normal directional
+input was released at the fourth destination change, then the target remained
+stationary for 32 advancing native frames. Polling observed every native frame.
+
+| Motion | ROM SHA-256 | Destination event frames | Three tile intervals |
