+{
+  "generator": "built-in image_gen",
+  "battle": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Taichung Quest full-body gym leader battle sprite, designed for a 64x64 logical pixel canvas and 15 opaque colors plus transparency. Create one original female leader Wenyi, a warm, observant contemporary Taiwanese temple architecture volunteer and educator, not a priest or a historical ruler. She is a young adult with dark brown hair in a neat low bun, small round glasses, a cream Mandarin-collar blouse, a muted cinnabar-red sleeveless vest with simple gold piping, dark teal straight trousers and flat dark shoes. She carries one small closed cream visitor notebook under her left arm and offers an open right palm, welcoming and confident. Her whole body and both shoes must be visible; 3/4 front pose facing viewer-left, compact expressive silhouette, head about one quarter of full height, like the established GBA game trainer portraits in the attached reference. Style: genuinely crisp coarse pixel art, thick dark contour, few solid shadow clusters, no smooth painted shading, no antialiasing, no text, no lettering, no watermark, no Pokemon, no invented ritual implements or religious costume. Transparent background, no ground shadow. Center a single figure with generous transparent margin. This is an in-game sprite, not a concept illustration. Reference image is only a style/scale reference, preserve no identity from it.",
+  "overworld": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Taichung Quest overworld walking sprite source sheet. Create the SAME Wenyi character as image 1, simplified to crisp GBA town-NPC pixel art as image 2. Dark brown low bun with a small gold tie, small round glasses on front view, cream blouse, cinnabar-red short sleeveless vest, dark teal trousers, dark flat shoes. No notebook extended to side: hold small cream notebook close to torso so she fits a 16x32 native cell, character target 14 pixels wide and 28 high. ONE TRANSPARENT 3x3 grid with NINE evenly spaced frames, equal cell sizes, no gridlines or text. Row1 exactly: facing SOUTH/front idle; facing SOUTH walk left foot forward; facing SOUTH walk right foot forward. Row2 exactly: facing NORTH/back idle; facing NORTH walk left foot forward; facing NORTH walk right foot forward. Row3 exactly: facing WEST/left profile idle; facing WEST walk left foot forward; facing WEST walk right foot forward. Whole body and shoes visible in each, fixed consistent character scale and head proportions, centered in each cell on matching baseline. Top-down 3/4 view with oversized game-NPC head, few flat shadow clusters, thick dark contours, coarse crisp pixels, no antialiasing, no painterly detail or smooth gradients. Keep hand, sleeve, vest, hair bun, face and pants coherent across directions. Transparent background; no ground shadows, extra people, names, labels, panels, borders or watermarks. This is an animation sheet, not concept art. Image1 identity reference; image2 native game sprite scale and row-independent pixel style reference.",
+  "postprocess": "Native technical export only: alpha threshold, nearest-neighbor fit, RGB555 15-color indexing, cell ordering and tile packing; no generated identity repaint."
+}
